  "result": "I've written the revised record to `record.jsonl` in the repair directory. It hasn't been through the validator or the gate yet.\n\n**What went wrong:** the gate failed `branch_1`. Three of the listed vehicle classes were mapped to legal-category memberships (authorized emergency vehicle, tow car, bus), and the run's reading leaves all three undecided. So every one of them reads unknown, and a transit bus on a signed shoulder could only come out unknown instead of compliant.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Public transit bus (e17):** it now uses the dedicated transit-bus class (`ru.transit_bus`) instead of \"bus category member and transit bus\". The ontology says to use a named class's own atom when one exists. The definition of \"bus\" covers every public transit bus, and its one exclusion (\"other than a taxicab\") is already built into that class.\n- **Permitted emergency vehicle and tow car (e13, e15):** I left these on their legal categories and added no stand-ins. Your validator rejected the readings I wrote for them last time, because a vehicle's class doesn't show a permit or an \"exclusively used for towing\" purpose. The justifications now say why no class replaces them, and that they stay unknown while the reading leaves them undecided.\n- **Scenarios:** `branch_1` is now a transit bus on a paved shoulder whose sign admits transit buses, expected compliant, which can now be decided. I added `branch_5`, an incident-management vehicle on a signed paved shoulder, also expected compliant.\n- **Smaller fixes:** the obligation text now says \"shoulder, median or divider\" in place of the coder's flagged \"every non-lane region\". I also dropped the proposal for `p.halt_speed_tolerance`, since that parameter is already in the catalogue.\n\n**Remaining risk:** while the reading leaves those three categories undecided, they can never decide a verdict, so they can only make one unknown. The mutation-adequacy check may flag them as never exercised. The real fix is in the run's reading, which is outside this record: it would need to mark the classes these definitions plainly cover as included. The coder suggested, for example, transit buses under \"bus\" and emergency vehicles or fire apparatus under \"authorized emergency vehicle\".",
